    "body": "Good call! 👍 \r\nNot something we have to address in this PR, but I think we may want to think about how we want to elegantly show warnings and alerts (configuration error, update available, etc). Because every prompt instance is stateless, it would print the error _every time_. 🤔 \r\n\r\nWhat would be the ideal way to inform the user that something is wrong with their configuration without getting in their way as they address it?\r\nIMO, the ideal solution would be to print a warning at the start of each session (3 hrs since the prompt was last used would be a fresh instance, for instance).",
